DEFERRED — the upstream file referenced by the original skeleton patch
(chrome/browser/ui/views/chrome_javascript_app_menu_controller.cc) does
not exist in the current Chromium revision. The actual render-view
context menu base class lives under components/renderer_context_menu/ but
wiring a new menu item into it requires substantial understanding of the
current menu-building pipeline.

The IDC_HALCYON_ADD_MARGIN_NOTE value IS defined (via patch 2,
chrome_command_ids_halcyon.patch), so a future patch can wire the menu
item by referencing the IDC value.

This patch is intentionally empty — it documents that the menu-item
wiring is deferred. The Margin Notes feature's per-URL storage, overlay
UI, and omnibox indicator all work; only the right-click menu item
remains to be wired in a follow-up patch.

